A Pure Type System (PTS) is a generalized typed lambda-calculus specified by a triple (S, A, R), where S is a set of sorts, A ⊆ S × S is a set of axioms, and R ⊆ S × S × S is a set of rules. The terms are generated by the grammar
  T ::= x | s | (T T) | (λx:T. T) | (Πx:T. T),
with s ∈ S and x a variable. Typing judgments Γ ⊢ M : A are derived using the standard PTS rules:
 (axiom) ⊢ s₁ : s₂ for (s₁, s₂) ∈ A;
 (start, weakening) extending contexts with well-formed types;
 (product) Γ ⊢ A : s₁ and Γ, x:A ⊢ B : s₂ with (s₁, s₂, s₃) ∈ R imply Γ ⊢ Πx:A.B : s₃;
 (application, abstraction) as usual;
 (conversion) using β-equality on types.
Reduction is β-reduction →_β on terms.

A typable term M (i.e., one with Γ ⊢ M : A for some Γ, A) is said to be weakly normalizing (WN) if there exists a finite β-reduction sequence from M to a β-normal form, and strongly normalizing (SN) if every β-reduction sequence from M is finite. A PTS is called weakly normalizing if every typable term is WN, and strongly normalizing if every typable term is SN.

Problem. Prove or refute: every weakly normalizing Pure Type System is strongly normalizing.

representations.original:
A Pure Type System (PTS) is a generalized typed lambda-calculus specified by a triple (S, A, R), where S is a set of sorts, A ⊆ S × S is a set of axioms, and R ⊆ S × S × S is a set of rules. The terms are generated by the grammar
  T ::= x | s | (T T) | (λx:T. T) | (Πx:T. T),
with s ∈ S and x a variable. Typing judgments Γ ⊢ M : A are derived using the standard PTS rules:
 (axiom) ⊢ s₁ : s₂ for (s₁, s₂) ∈ A;
 (start, weakening) extending contexts with well-formed types;
 (product) Γ ⊢ A : s₁ and Γ, x:A ⊢ B : s₂ with (s₁, s₂, s₃) ∈ R imply Γ ⊢ Πx:A.B : s₃;
 (application, abstraction) as usual;
 (conversion) using β-equality on types.
Reduction is β-reduction →_β on terms.

A typable term M (i.e., one with Γ ⊢ M : A for some Γ, A) is said to be weakly normalizing (WN) if there exists a finite β-reduction sequence from M to a β-normal form, and strongly normalizing (SN) if every β-reduction sequence from M is finite. A PTS is called weakly normalizing if every typable term is WN, and strongly normalizing if every typable term is SN.

Problem. Prove or refute: every weakly normalizing Pure Type System is strongly normalizing.

