Consider integral compact symplectic 4-manifolds, i.e., pairs $(X,\omega)$ where $X$ is a closed smooth 4-manifold and $\omega$ is a symplectic form on $X$ whose cohomology class $[\omega] \in H^2(X;\mathbb{R})$ lies in the image of $H^2(X;\mathbb{Z})$. Two such pairs $(X_1,\omega_1)$ and $(X_2,\omega_2)$ are symplectically equivalent if there exists a diffeomorphism $\phi : X_1 \to X_2$ with $\phi^*\omega_2 = \omega_1$. To any such $(X,\omega)$ associate:
(i) the fundamental group $\pi_1(X)$;
(ii) the Chern classes $c_1, c_2 \in H^*(X;\mathbb{Z})$ of the tangent bundle $TX$ (equipped with an almost complex structure compatible with $\omega$, which is unique up to homotopy);
(iii) the four numerical invariants $c_1^2[X]$, $c_2[X]$, $(c_1 \cup [\omega])[X]$, and $([\omega]\cup[\omega])[X]$, where $[X]$ is the fundamental class.

Problem: Fix a group $G$ and a quadruple of integers $(a,b,c,d)$. Classify, up to symplectic equivalence, all integral compact symplectic 4-manifolds $(X,\omega)$ with $\pi_1(X) \cong G$ and $(c_1^2[X], c_2[X], (c_1\cup[\omega])[X], [\omega]^2[X]) = (a,b,c,d)$.

