Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p > 0$. A "big action" is a pair $(C,G)$ consisting of a smooth projective connected curve $C/k$ of genus $g_C \geq 2$ together with a finite $p$-subgroup $G \subseteq \mathrm{Aut}_k(C)$ satisfying the following condition (N):

(i) there exists a (necessarily unique) point $\infty \in C$ such that $G$ is contained in the stabilizer $\mathrm{Aut}_k(C)_\infty$ of $\infty$;
(ii) the quotient $C/G$ has genus $0$;
(iii) the ratio $|G|/g_C$ is strictly greater than $\tfrac{2p}{p-1}$.

For such a pair, let $G = G_0 \supseteq G_1 \supseteq G_2 \supseteq \cdots$ denote the lower ramification filtration of $G$ at the fixed point $\infty$ (defined via the valuation of the local ring $\mathcal{O}_{C,\infty}$). The group $G_2$ is the second lower ramification group at $\infty$.

Problem. Classify, up to isomorphism, all big actions $(C,G)$ satisfying condition (N) for which the second lower ramification group $G_2$ is an elementary abelian $p$-group, i.e., isomorphic to $(\mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z})^r$ for some $r \geq 1$. In particular, describe the possible Artin–Schreier(–Witt) equations defining such curves $C$ as $G$-covers of $\mathbb{P}^1_k$, and the resulting structure of $G$.

